All 15 tests pass — 10 failures → 0 failures. Here's a summary of every fix:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs)
- `has_permission`: comparison was case-sensitive (`required in user_roles`). Fixed by lowercasing both sides via `required.lower() in (r.lower() for r in user_roles)`.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` — denied admins who aren't the owner and owners who aren't admins. Changed to `or`.

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` was shared across all instances — two inventories appeared to share storage. Changed to `None` + fresh dict per call, with a `dict(initial)` copy to avoid mutating the caller's dict.
- `add`: overwrote stock (`self._stock[sku] = qty`) instead of accumulating. Changed to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- `reserve`: rejected reserving exactly the available amount (`qty >= self.available(sku)`). Changed to `qty > self.available(sku)` so reserving all stock is allowed.
- `release`: allowed reserved count to go negative. Added a `current - qty < 0` check that raises `ValueError`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs)
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase — `"Hello"` stayed `"Hello"`. Added `char.lower()` before classification.
- `slugify`: `"hello---world".replace("--", "-")` only collapses one pair, leaving `"hello--world"`. Replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)` to collapse any run of dashes.
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` could exceed `max_len` (e.g. 10 + 1 = 11). Changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`.
